# What Vercel is allowed to serve.
#
# The repo being private stops GitHub exposure; it does NOT stop Vercel, which
# serves every deployed file to anyone with the URL. These three carry the book
# and must not be deployed. They stay in the repo — the engine and Cowork still
# read them — they just stop being published.
outputs/trades.json
outputs/fact_pack.json
outputs/trade_metrics.json

# Never requested by the browser, and they make every deployment bigger
# (deployment storage is the limit the Vercel email was about).
*.py
*.pyc
__pycache__/
*.csv
*.db
*.zip
.github/
tests/
test_*.py
requirements.txt
outputs/oge/
outputs/history/
outputs/*_seen.json
outputs/sec_cik_map.json
outputs/iv_history.json

